1
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:04,240
Down here!

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:06,377
My Harmon will hit you all the harder!

3
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:07,290
Underwater...

4
00:00:07,373 --> 00:00:09,577
turquoise blue...

5
00:00:09,660 --> 00:00:11,040
OVERDRIVE!

6
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:18,977
He did it! Bravo!

7
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,380
That was amazing!

8
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:21,980
It's not over yet!

9
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:26,337
I can't believe Bluford was able
to dodge that blast of Harmon.

10
00:00:26,420 --> 00:00:27,857
He moved so fast underwater.

11
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:29,420
He was all a blur.

12
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,647
My overdrive barely
clansed off his forehead.

13
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:36,357
Now I know anything
less than a solid punch

14
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:39,087
won't be enough to send
the Hormone into him.

15
00:00:39,240 --> 00:00:42,900
My good Lord Dio, I thank
thee for this life anew,

16
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:45,417
that I may duel with
this stout-hearted lad.

17
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:48,437
My heart would swell to
bursting if it still beats.

18
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:51,220
In blood and deed, he
is the stuff of heroes.

19
00:00:51,900 --> 00:00:54,620
Now we will fight in our native element.

20
00:00:55,060 --> 00:00:59,900
It is by mastery of our arts and strength
of our spirits that we wage this duel.

21
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:01,880
Bear your soul.

22
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:05,432
Hold nothing back lest you not
survive beyond this moment.

23
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:11,940
Even as Dio's puppet, his pride
is a force to be reckoned with.

24
00:01:12,160 --> 00:01:16,037
But his knightly valor has been
twisted into a wanton love of violence.

25
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:19,061
When I best you, I'll take
your head as my trophy.

26
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:20,997
It's easy to let your hair do the work.

27
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:24,200
Come, withstand my hormone
face to face like a man.

28
00:01:36,360 --> 00:01:37,800
Let's go.

29
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:45,590
Yeah, Joe!

30
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:03,300
Overtry Barrage!

31
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:12,700
Joe Joe!

32
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:21,540
This is terrible.

33
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:24,997
Harmon can only be projected
through the arms and the legs.

34
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:27,337
With his arms bound in
front of him like that,

35
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:31,017
he has no way of blasting through
that infernal hair of Bluford's.

36
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:34,982
I want to help him out, but you
and me have got things even worse.

37
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:38,140
I think old Tarkus fancies a dust-up.

38
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:45,840
This hair, it's tearing through
my clothes, through my skin.

39
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:50,513
The more I struggle, the tighter it
winds, and it's sucking my blood away.

40
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,780
Beat your petty life a-due!

41
00:03:58,020 --> 00:03:59,500
Behold the coup de grace!

42
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:03,964
I'll take your head and bathe in
a fountain of life-giving blood!

43
00:04:04,840 --> 00:04:05,920
Take this!

44
00:04:12,940 --> 00:04:15,357
Watch this not all that conducts hormones.

45
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:17,620
Metal, silver, overdrive!

46
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,180
What a brain!

47
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:24,337
Using his sword to hoist Bluford
by his own bleeding petard!

48
00:04:24,420 --> 00:04:25,538
Who thinks of that?

49
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:30,560
How my heart resonates!

50
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:33,460
I'm pulsing with heat and life!

51
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:38,720
My very blood is a symphony within me!

52
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:43,040
Sunlight, yellow, overdrive!

53
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:47,220
There we go, that's it!

54
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:50,560
About time we heard the
welcome crackle of Harmoon.

55
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:56,457
When I pummeled Bluford a moment
ago, something felt different.

56
00:04:56,540 --> 00:04:59,897
Knowing his past makes his
present corruption all the worse.

57
00:04:59,980 --> 00:05:01,180
Take heart, Jojo.

58
00:05:01,460 --> 00:05:02,977
He is that man no longer.

59
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:06,800
He's nothing but a zombie,
eager to spread his evil.

60
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:09,420
You must be the one to end him.

61
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:15,920
Boy, I'm a black knight, Bluford.

62
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:18,140
Strike me as thou wilt.

63
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:19,635
This pain is nothing.

64
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:23,240
He's still dangerous, mate. Look out.

65
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:27,837
He's been missing an arm
and scorched all the hell.

66
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:30,720
He's laying into Jojo
every bit as ferociously.

67
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:35,530
What the?

68
00:05:35,613 --> 00:05:36,917
Don't just stand there!

69
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:37,830
Do something!

70
00:05:38,060 --> 00:05:41,413
If you don't get out of there
now, it's curtains for you!

71
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:49,597
Have they both gone mad?

72
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:51,151
What are they doing, huh?

73
00:05:53,660 --> 00:05:54,900
A moment to go.

74
00:05:55,160 --> 00:05:57,017
You said this pain is nothing.

75
00:05:57,100 --> 00:06:00,580
That means pain is something
you can feel again.

76
00:06:03,060 --> 00:06:06,960
Oh, the flowers, they're
blooming all around him.

77
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:12,540
Even now, the Hormone ravages the evil
that animates Bluford's long dead corpse.

78
00:06:17,340 --> 00:06:19,920
You see, the long
forgotten pain came back.

79
00:06:20,260 --> 00:06:22,600
Only humans know that sort of ache.

80
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:25,040
Observe, my dear Speedwagon.

81
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:27,613
His zombie body succumbs to the Hormone,

82
00:06:27,780 --> 00:06:30,920
but his noble soul is
redeemed in the process. Yes.

83
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:32,857
I could sense the good in you.

84
00:06:32,940 --> 00:06:34,881
That's why I didn't try to dodge.

85
00:06:35,740 --> 00:06:39,269
You could have killed me just
now, but you stayed your hand.

86
00:06:39,820 --> 00:06:40,960
Look at his face.

87
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:44,977
It's like all the rage and hatred he
had when Dio brought him back are gone.

88
00:06:45,060 --> 00:06:49,517
His features are so gentle he could be a
bloke catching up with his oldest mate.

89
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:53,800
You stood there like a statue,
ready to take the fatal blow.

90
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:57,780
Oblivion beckoned, but
you put your trust in me.

91
00:06:58,540 --> 00:07:00,920
Your faith in human goodness is rare.

92
00:07:04,560 --> 00:07:07,320
Once I have railed
against the pain I feel.

93
00:07:07,940 --> 00:07:11,900
Now, going to my rightful end, I
cherish all that proves me human.

94
00:07:12,580 --> 00:07:14,160
It gives me joy.

95
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:18,020
The embers dull within
me, but I am tranquil.

96
00:07:18,940 --> 00:07:21,240
There is no bitterness left.

97
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:24,160
What irony to live yet again,

98
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:28,880
dying with thanks on my lips for
the very man who slaughters me anew.

99
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:31,920
I shall return to my one true master.

100
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:38,620
I would know the name of
the warrior who bested me.

101
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:40,980
Would you kindly do me that honor?

102
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:43,840
It's Jonathan Joestar.

103
00:07:45,280 --> 00:07:46,380
Sir Jonathan,

104
00:07:46,820 --> 00:07:49,337
I leave you this sword given to me by my

105
00:07:49,420 --> 00:07:52,067
precious queen and the
word engraved upon it.

106
00:07:52,900 --> 00:07:53,730
Luck.

107
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:58,140
But first, let me affix
my own benediction.

108
00:07:59,320 --> 00:08:00,150
Pluck.

109
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:02,260
Sir Bluefoot!

110
00:08:10,320 --> 00:08:12,020
Go you to your rest.

111
00:08:12,300 --> 00:08:15,006
Let no one doubt you
have earned it, Bluefoot.

112
00:08:15,660 --> 00:08:16,490
Why?

113
00:08:16,880 --> 00:08:19,998
Why did I have to strike
him down to redeem his soul?

114
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:25,400
He died once before with hate in his
heart, but his spirit was still pure.

115
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:30,160
He returned not out of choice
but dragged above by Dio's evil.

116
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:32,600
His evil in the mosque's power.

117
00:08:32,900 --> 00:08:35,606
I will send them both
to hell before the dawn.

118
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:38,340
Jojo, he's right behind you.

119
00:08:39,020 --> 00:08:39,850
Tarkus.

120
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:44,520
You villain.

121
00:08:44,860 --> 00:08:47,977
That was the armor of a
steadfast friend and comrade.

122
00:08:48,060 --> 00:08:49,900
He died with honor and dignity.

123
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:52,317
He died like a spineless dog.

124
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:54,740
He was too clever by half.

125
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:57,057
Liked winning his fights with thinking.

126
00:08:57,140 --> 00:08:59,820
I just hit him until they fall to pieces.

127
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:02,724
What use have I got for clever?

128
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:05,400
I carry a sword as tall as a man.

129
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:08,139
None of you will get an easy death.

130
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:24,680
Jojo, nice catch.

131
00:09:26,400 --> 00:09:27,940
The cliff is crumbling!

132
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,400
These dead leaves...

133
00:09:33,140 --> 00:09:34,740
Jojo! Yes, sir!

134
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:42,220
Life magnetism overdrive!

135
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:54,240
Hurry, Poco! Speedwagon! Grab on!

136
00:10:01,420 --> 00:10:04,480
All human beings, whether
adept at Hamon or not,

137
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:07,080
constantly exude a weak magnetic field.

138
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:10,441
An overdrive can increase
the power of that field.

139
00:10:10,940 --> 00:10:15,822
Jojo and Zeppeli sent it into the leaves,
drawing them together into a solid sheet.

140
00:10:16,460 --> 00:10:17,290
Wow!

141
00:10:18,020 --> 00:10:18,850
Bye!

142
00:10:22,940 --> 00:10:23,880
We're flying!

143
00:10:24,160 --> 00:10:25,278
I can't believe it!

144
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:27,127
I bet you're magicians, huh?

145
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:28,577
You'd have to be, right?

146
00:10:28,660 --> 00:10:31,917
How did you learn to do all of these
neat spells in the first place?

147
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:33,140
Damn good question!

148
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:36,437
I've been watching them do
it and I still pinch myself!

149
00:10:36,520 --> 00:10:37,350
Oi, Baron!

150
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:38,477
What's the story?

151
00:10:38,560 --> 00:10:40,031
We're not going anywhere!

152
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:43,321
How on earth did you pick
up all this mumbo-jumbo?

153
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:57,560
Many years ago, my travels took me to
India, where I discovered a mysterious man.

154
00:10:58,200 --> 00:10:59,960
He called himself a doctor,

155
00:11:00,260 --> 00:11:03,777
though he was very young and
lacked all the tools of the trade.

156
00:11:03,860 --> 00:11:07,557
Little did I know, he was more potent
of a medic than I'd ever encountered.

157
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:12,240
He took a gangrenous limb in his hands
and healed it with light from within.

158
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:15,220
That was the day I learned of Hamon.

159
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:19,537
I'd been looking for something with
which to fight the stone mask's evil,

160
00:11:19,620 --> 00:11:21,520
and in Hamon, I had found it.

161
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:23,220
Eager to learn,

162
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:25,977
I crossed into Tibet
and up the Salween River

163
00:11:26,060 --> 00:11:29,020
in search of he who had
taught the young healer.

164
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:38,020
His name was Tonpetty

165
00:11:51,520 --> 00:11:52,350
Stranger,

166
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:56,877
these eyes of mine have
seen your future If

167
00:11:56,960 --> 00:12:00,280
you pursue the mysteries
of Harmon as my pupil,

168
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:02,020
your fate is sealed.

169
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:06,080
The day will come when this
will be the death of you.

170
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:09,097
I understand.

171
00:12:09,180 --> 00:12:12,980
If I must die to end this quest, so be it.

172
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:23,877
Master Tonpedi's prophecy
is never far from

173
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:27,300
my mind But I cannot
tell them Not even Jojo

174
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:28,910
Baron?

175
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:32,740
So, that sound?

176
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:35,788
That's part of Halmon
doing its thing, yeah?

177
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:38,980
Hardly Look out, it's Tarkus!

178
00:12:49,260 --> 00:12:50,220
He's insane!

179
00:12:50,540 --> 00:12:53,834
Leaping from that height just
to give chase to his foes!

180
00:12:56,720 --> 00:13:00,377
There's a goodly amount of Hormone
holding these leaves together, you brute.

181
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:02,578
Painful to the touch for the United.

182
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:04,090
What's that?

183
00:13:04,180 --> 00:13:07,097
That's where the knights used
to train in the olden days.

184
00:13:07,180 --> 00:13:08,597
Leap to safety, everyone!

185
00:13:08,680 --> 00:13:10,856
Before we get swatted out of the sky!

186
00:13:17,580 --> 00:13:21,277
Crazy Blighter, he just slammed
himself straight into the tower.

187
00:13:21,360 --> 00:13:24,654
Yes, and thank your lucky
stars that he did, Speedwagon.

188
00:13:25,060 --> 00:13:26,236
Unlike their master,

189
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:31,186
Dio's minions can't regenerate, so that
should be the last we see of that beast.

190
00:13:37,260 --> 00:13:38,090
How did...

191
00:13:38,173 --> 00:13:39,433
he should be mincemeat.

192
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:41,657
Even in death he has a will of iron.

193
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:44,520
How does his body endure
under such punishment?

194
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:46,260
He's climbing up!

195
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:50,020
We can't destroy Dio while
this monster dogs our steps.

196
00:13:50,300 --> 00:13:52,241
It seems we have no other choice.

197
00:13:52,460 --> 00:13:54,578
Tarkus meets his doom here and now.

198
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:57,400
Jojo, this will be perilous.

199
00:13:57,620 --> 00:13:59,326
Get the lad to safety within.

200
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:15,720
This door, something's odd about it.

201
00:14:16,140 --> 00:14:20,157
Be careful, this is where they used to
train the knights how to kill people.

202
00:14:20,240 --> 00:14:22,240
They say it's full of booby traps.

203
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:26,420
Doc Jojo, something's coming at ya!

204
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:31,110
Jojo!

205
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:36,500
Who ensnared me?

206
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:40,610
Sorokas!

207
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:45,380
Yes, caught you good, your
fleet of foot, little man.

208
00:14:45,580 --> 00:14:48,227
But now you and me are
chained to each other.

209
00:14:48,380 --> 00:14:49,909
You've got nowhere to run.

210
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:56,057
Jojo had wandered into the
lair of the Two-Headed Dragon,

211
00:14:56,140 --> 00:14:59,617
an ancient sparring ground and
home of the Chain Deathmatch.

212
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:05,320
I killed 48 men here, taking a
life's an art form, and I'm a master.

213
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:11,937
that's enough you can't
punch through it that door is

214
00:15:12,020 --> 00:15:16,277
solid iron goodness he's batted
his knuckles bloody against

215
00:15:16,360 --> 00:15:20,297
it hormone is very versatile
but it's meant to be used as

216
00:15:20,380 --> 00:15:23,577
a rapier not as a sledge
hammer bricks i could beat to a

217
00:15:23,660 --> 00:15:27,457
powder but this door is too
strong jojo faces a darker

218
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:30,697
dilemma that chain about his
neck is more than ripple energy

219
00:15:30,780 --> 00:15:34,837
can overcome breaking out of
that collar is impossible and

220
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:38,220
you'll need the key to unlock
it too bad it's right here

221
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:43,957
during a deathmatch the door to the
outside is fashioned to lock tight

222
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:48,275
just as I have the key to your collar
you have the one that goes to mine

223
00:15:49,100 --> 00:15:51,577
therefore the only way
that either of us is going

224
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:56,600
to get out of here is by
taking the other's head

225
00:16:09,560 --> 00:16:11,913
The chain is touching the stone ceiling,

226
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:15,002
so the Hormone lacks a
direct path into Tarkus!

227
00:16:21,900 --> 00:16:24,160
He's broken the bone in my forearm!

228
00:16:25,360 --> 00:16:26,980
It's a simple thing to fix,

229
00:16:27,260 --> 00:16:30,817
a little Hormone and I'm good as
new, But in order to use Hormone,

230
00:16:30,900 --> 00:16:33,500
I need to be free of this damnable collar!

231
00:16:33,860 --> 00:16:35,140
I can't breathe!

232
00:16:39,300 --> 00:16:40,130
Jojo!

233
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:41,920
Oh no!

234
00:16:42,260 --> 00:16:45,142
This is all so frightening,
I think I wet myself!

235
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:48,620
This village was safe
until these men arrived.

236
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:50,078
I'm in danger here.

237
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:53,817
You need to get away from all this
fighting with the Double Pogo.

238
00:16:53,900 --> 00:16:55,677
I see a lever, Baron Zeppeli.

239
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:59,517
No telling for certain, but I think
pulling on it will open this door.

240
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:02,257
Fighting Tarkus is a daunting
enough task as it is,

241
00:17:02,340 --> 00:17:05,634
never mind doing it fresh out
of a battle with Blueford.

242
00:17:06,140 --> 00:17:07,477
Come, hella high water.

243
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:10,384
We must find a way to get
in there and help him.

244
00:17:11,240 --> 00:17:13,475
It's locked up tighter than a nunnery.

245
00:17:18,860 --> 00:17:19,960
It's so narrow.

246
00:17:20,880 --> 00:17:23,939
Try as they might, they
could never squeeze through.

247
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:25,870
But...

248
00:17:27,660 --> 00:17:28,940
Maybe I could.

249
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:33,870
Blast it!

250
